"### Using a Global Variable in a Function\n\n```python\ndef use_global_variable():\n    x = 10  # Define the global variable here\n\ndef modify_global_variable():\n    global x  # Specify that x is a global variable\n    x = 20\n\nuse_global_variable()\nprint(x)  # Output: 20\n\nmodify_global_variable()\nprint(x)  # Output: 20\n\n# Changing the global variable inside another function\ndef update_global_variable():\n    global x\n    x = 30\n\nupdate_global_variable()\nprint(x)  # Output: 30\n```\n\n### Using a Global Variable Defined in One Function Inside Another Function\n\n```python\ndef define_global_variable():\n    global outer_x  # Specify that outer_x is a global variable\n    outer_x = 10\n\ndef inner_function():\n    global outer_x  # Specify that outer_x is a global variable\n    outer_x += 5\n\ndefine_global_variable()\nprint(outer_x)  # Output: 15\n\ninner_function()\nprint(outer_x)  # Output: 20\n```"
