"```python\ndef explain_null_blank_difference():\n    print(\"Django Model Field Null and Blank Difference\")\n    print(\"------------------------------------------------\")\n\n    print(\"1. null=True only\")\n    print(\"This option makes the field nullable, allowing values to be None.\")\n    print(\"Advantages: allows for missing or null values, can be used with some database types.\")\n    print(\"Disadvantages: does not prevent empty strings from being entered, can lead to inconsistent data.\")\n\n    print(\"\\n2. blank=True only\")\n    print(\"This option makes the field blank, allowing empty strings to be entered.\")\n    print(\"Advantages: prevents empty strings from being entered, can be used with some database types.\")\n    print(\"Disadvantages: does not prevent null values from being entered, can lead to inconsistent data.\")\n\n    print(\"\\n3. null=True and blank=True\")\n    print(\"This option makes both the field nullable and blank.\")\n    print(\"Advantages: prevents both null and empty string values, can be used with most database types.\")\n    print(\"Disadvantages: can lead to data loss if no value is entered, may be more restrictive than needed for some fields.\")\n\nexplain_null_blank_difference()\n```"
