"### Image File Types Comparison\n\n#### Overview\nWhen building websites or interfaces, choosing the right image file type is crucial for optimal performance, compatibility, and visual quality. This guide will cover the key differences between PNG, GIF, JPEG, and SVG, helping you decide when to use each.\n\n#### Image File Types\n\n#### PNG\n- **Lossless compression**: Preserves image quality without any data loss.\n- **Transparency**: Supports transparent backgrounds, making it ideal for icons, logos, and graphics.\n- **Color depth**: Supports up to 16 million colors.\n- **Use cases**:\n  - Logos and icons with transparent backgrounds.\n  - Images with text or graphics that require high color accuracy.\n  - Web graphics and images that require lossless compression.\n\n#### GIF\n- **Lossless compression**: Preserves image quality without any data loss.\n- **Animation support**: Can be used for animated images, making it suitable for loading animations or banners.\n- **Color depth**: Supports up to 256 colors.\n- **Use cases**:\n  - Animations and loading animations.\n  - Simple graphics and icons.\n  - Web banners and advertisements.\n\n#### JPEG\n- **Lossy compression**: May result in a loss of image quality, especially when compressing high-resolution images.\n- **Color depth**: Supports up to 16 million colors.\n- **Use cases**:\n  - Photographic images where some loss of quality is acceptable.\n  - Images that require fast loading times.\n\n#### SVG\n- **Vector graphics**: Uses mathematical equations to draw shapes, resulting in scalable and resolution-independent images.\n- **No compression**: Preserves image quality without any data loss.\n- **Use cases**:\n  - Logos and icons that need to be scaled without losing quality.\n  - Web graphics and images that require high resolution and scalability.\n  - Vector-based illustrations and diagrams.\n\n#### Comparison Summary\n\n| File Type | Lossless/lossy | Transparency | Color Depth | Use Cases |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| PNG | Lossless | Yes | Up to 16M | Logos, icons, graphics |\n| GIF | Lossless | No | Up to 256 | Animations, simple graphics |\n| JPEG | Lossy | No | Up to 16M | Photographic images, fast loading |\n| SVG | No compression | No | No limit | Logos, icons, vector graphics |\n\n#### Recommendation\nIf you don't care about each and every pixel, JPEG might be the \"lightest\" option due to its lossy compression. However, consider the specific requirements of your project. If you prioritize image quality and scalability, use PNG or SVG. For animations, GIF is a suitable choice."
"from flask import Flask, render_template, request, redirect, url_for, session\nfrom flask_session import Session\nimport sqlite3\nimport hashlib\nimport secrets\nimport os\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\napp.config[\"SESSION_PERMANENT\"] = False\napp.config[\"SESSION_TYPE\"] = \"filesystem\"\nSession(app)\n\n# Connect to SQLite database\nconn = sqlite3.connect(\"users.db\")\nc = conn.cursor()\n\n# Create table\nc.execute('''CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users\n             (username text, password text, email text)''')\nconn.commit()\n\ndef hash_password(password):\n    return hashlib.sha256(password.encode()).hexdigest()\n\ndef verify_password(stored_password, provided_password):\n    return stored_password == hash_password(provided_password)\n\ndef generate_token(length):\n    return secrets.token_urlsafe(length)\n\ndef get_user(username):\n    c.execute(\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = ?\", (username,))\n    user = c.fetchone()\n    return user\n\n@app.route(\"/\")\ndef index():\n    return render_template(\"index.html\")\n\n@app.route(\"/login\", methods=[\"GET\", \"POST\"])\ndef login():\n    if request.method == \"POST\":\n        username = request.form[\"username\"]\n        password = request.form[\"password\"]\n        user = get_user(username)\n        if user and verify_password(user[1], password):\n            session[\"username\"] = username\n            return redirect(url_for(\"protected\"))\n        else:\n            return render_template(\"login.html\")\n    return render_template(\"login.html\")\n\n@app.route(\"/logout\")\ndef logout():\n    session.pop(\"username\", None)\n    return redirect(url_for(\"index\"))\n\n@app.route(\"/register\", methods=[\"GET\", \"POST\"])\ndef register():\n    if request.method == \"POST\":\n        username = request.form[\"username\"]\n        password = request.form[\"password\"]\n        email = request.form[\"email\"]\n        c.execute(\"INSERT INTO users VALUES (?, ?, ?)\",\n                  (username, hash_password(password), email))\n        conn.commit()\n        return redirect(url_for(\"login\"))\n    return render_template(\"register.html\")\n\n@app.route(\"/protected\")\ndef protected():\n    if \"username\" in session:\n        return render_template(\"protected.html\")\n    return redirect(url_for(\"login\"))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    app.run(debug=True)"
