"# Development Server Options in Ruby on Rails\n\n### Overview\n\nRuby on Rails provides several development server options. Here's a brief overview of the most commonly used ones:\n\n- **WEBrick**: A built-in server that comes with Ruby. It's simple to set up but not ideal for production use.\n\n- **Mongrel**: Another built-in server. It's more efficient than WEBrick but still not suitable for production environments.\n\n- **Passenger**: A third-party server that simplifies the deployment process. It doesn't replace Mongrel but can be used in conjunction with it.\n\n- **Apache/Nginx**: Web servers that can be used to host Rails applications in production. They're not development servers but can be used with development servers.\n\n### Development Server Setup\n\nFor a simple development setup, you can use Mongrel. However, since you want to test SSL, consider using a more advanced setup.\n\n```python\n# Mongrel\nrequire 'mongrel'\nMongrel::Server.new(\n  :port => 8000,\n  :options => {\n    :ssl => true,\n    :ssl_key => 'path/to/key',\n    :ssl_cert => 'path/to/cert'\n  }\n).start\n```\n\n### Passenger Setup\n\nIf you want a more advanced setup, consider using Passenger. It's not a replacement for Mongrel but can be used in conjunction with it.\n\n```python\n# Passenger\nrequire 'passenger'\nPassenger::Util.start_app('/path/to/your/app')\n```\n\n### Capistrano Setup\n\nCapistrano is a deployment tool, not a development server. It can be used to deploy your application to a production environment.\n\n```python\n# Capistrano\nrequire 'capistrano'\nCapistrano::Config::Settings.default_path = '/etc/capistrano'\n```\n\n### Apache/Nginx Setup\n\nThese are web servers that can be used to host Rails applications in production. They're not development servers but can be used with development servers.\n\n```python\n# Apache\nrequire 'httparty'\nrequire 'rubygems'\ngem 'httparty'\nrequire 'rake'\nrake 'apache2:install'\nrake 'apache2:start'\n\n# Nginx\nrequire 'rake'\nrake 'nginx:install'\nrake 'nginx:start'\n```\n\n### Recommended Setup\n\nFor testing SSL, consider using a more advanced setup like Passenger with a reverse proxy like Nginx.\n\n```python\n# Passenger with Nginx\nrequire 'passenger'\nrequire 'rake'\nrake 'passenger:install'\nrake 'passenger:start'\n```\n\nThis setup provides a more robust and secure way to test SSL. However, it's overkill for simple development environments. Mongrel with SSL support is still a viable option.\n\n```python\n# Mongrel with SSL\nrequire 'mongrel'\nMongrel::Server.new(\n  :port => 8000,\n  :options => {\n    :ssl => true,\n    :ssl_key => 'path/to/key',\n    :ssl_cert => 'path/to/cert'\n  }\n).start\n```"
