"# Prevent Excel from Automatically Converting Text to Dates\n\nTo prevent Excel from automatically converting certain text values to dates, you can use the `text` attribute in your CSV file.\n\n```python\nimport csv\n\n# Define the CSV writer\nwriter = csv.writer(open('output.csv', 'w'))\n\n# Define the fieldnames with the text attribute\nfieldnames = ['field1', 'field2', 'field3']\nwriter.writerow(fieldnames)\n\n# Write rows with the text attribute\nrow = ['text', '2022-01-01', '2022-02-01']\nwriter.writerow(row)\n```\n\nIn this example, the `text` attribute is used in the second row. This tells Excel not to try to convert the value to a date.\n\nNote: The `text` attribute is specific to the CSV format and is not a standard attribute in Python's `csv` module. However, it works in Excel when reading the CSV file."
