"```python\ndef delete_item(dictionary, key):\n    return {k: v for k, v in dictionary.items() if k != key}\n\ndef delete_key(dictionary, key):\n    return {k: v for k, v in dictionary.items() if k != key}\n\n# Example usage:\noriginal_dict = {\"a\": 1, \"b\": 2, \"c\": 3}\nprint(\"Original dictionary:\", original_dict)\n\n# Delete item by key\nnew_dict = delete_item(original_dict, \"b\")\nprint(\"Dictionary without 'b':\", new_dict)\n\n# Delete key that may not exist\nnew_dict = delete_key(original_dict, \"d\")\nprint(\"Dictionary without 'd':\", new_dict)\n```"
