"import tensorflow as tf\n\n# logits is a tensor that represents the raw output of a neural network.\n# It's a probability distribution over all possible classes in the dataset.\n\n# softmax normalizes the output of the neural network so that it sums up to 1.\n# This is useful for classification problems where we want to predict the probability of each class.\n\n# softmax_cross_entropy_with_logits calculates the cross-entropy loss between the predicted probabilities and the true labels.\n# This is useful for training neural networks on classification problems.\n\nlogits = tf.constant([[0.1, 0.2, 0.7], [0.4, 0.6, 0.0]])  # example logits\n\n# Example usage of softmax\nsoftmax_output = tf.nn.softmax(logits)\nprint(softmax_output)\n\n# Example usage of softmax_cross_entropy_with_logits\nlabels = tf.constant([[0, 0, 1], [1, 0, 0]])  # example labels\ncross_entropy_loss = tf.nn.softmax_cross_entropy_with_logits(logits=logits, labels=labels)\nprint(cross_entropy_loss)"
