"def pair_socks(socks):\n    socks.sort()\n    pairs = []\n    i = 0\n    while i < len(socks):\n        if i + 1 < len(socks) and socks[i] == socks[i+1]:\n            pairs.append(socks[i])\n            i += 2\n        else:\n            i += 1\n    return pairsassistant\n\nThis function sorts the socks, then iterates over the list, pairing each sock with its matching partner. If the current sock doesn't have a matching partner, it simply moves on to the next sock. This solution has a time complexity of O(N log N) due to the sorting step, and a space complexity of O(N) for the output list."
