"# SQL Injection Explanation\n\nThe SQL injection attack in the \"Bobby Tables\" XKCD comic works as follows:\n\n```python\nsql_command = \"SELECT * FROM students WHERE name = '\" + \"Robert'; DROP TABLE STUDENTS; --\"\n```\n\nIn this example, the user input is used directly in the SQL command without any proper sanitization or escaping. The SQL command is vulnerable to injection because of the semicolon (`;`) and the `--` comment characters.\n\nWhen the SQL parser encounters a semicolon, it expects the end of a SQL statement. However, in this case, the semicolon is followed by the `--` comment characters, which tell the parser to ignore the rest of the line. This effectively bypasses the parser and allows the attacker to execute additional SQL commands.\n\n```python\n# Example of how the SQL parser would interpret the SQL command\n# The semicolon is ignored, and the rest of the line is treated as a comment\nsql_command = \"SELECT * FROM students WHERE name = 'Robert'; DROP TABLE STUDENTS; --\"\n```\n\nAs a result, the `DROP TABLE STUDENTS` command is executed, deleting the entire `STUDENTS` table.\n\nTo prevent such attacks, it is essential to use parameterized queries or prepared statements, which separate the SQL code from the user input, ensuring that the input is properly sanitized and escaped."
