"```python\nimport threading\nimport queue\n\nclass BackgroundWorker:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.queue = queue.Queue()\n\n    def DoWork(self, worker):\n        self.queue.put(\"Message to worker\")\n\n    def run(self, message):\n        self.queue.put(message)\n\n    def get_message(self):\n        return self.queue.get()\n\n\ndef main():\n    bw = BackgroundWorker()\n\n    bw_thread = threading.Thread(target=bw.run, args=(\"Message to worker\",))\n    bw_thread.start()\n\n    bw_thread.join()\n\n    message = bw.get_message()\n    print(message)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\nThis code uses a queue to communicate between the main thread and the worker thread, which allows the `FacebookApplication.FacebookFriendsList` creation to be performed on the worker thread. The `run` method is called on the worker thread, and the `get_message` method is used to retrieve the message sent by the `run` method."
