"```python\n# No code is required to answer the question as it's a Kubernetes configuration issue.\n```\n\nThe issue here is that the `imagePullPolicy` is set to `Always`, which means the image should always be re-pulled when the rolling update is performed. However, the `imagePullSecrets` are not being used. Instead, the image is being pulled from a repository directly specified in the `image` field.\n\nTo force Kubernetes to re-pull the image, you can update the `imagePullPolicy` to `Always` and remove the `imagePullSecrets` field. Here's the updated configuration:\n\n```yml\napiVersion: v1\nkind: ReplicationController\nmetadata:\n  name: myapp\n  labels:\n    app: myapp\nspec:\n  replicas: 2\n  selector:\n    app: myapp\n    deployment: initial\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      labels:\n        app: myapp\n        deployment: initial\n    spec:\n      containers:\n      - name: myapp\n        image: myregistry.com/myapp:5c3dda6b\n        ports:\n        - containerPort: 80\n      imagePullPolicy: Always\n```\n\nThis will ensure that the image is always re-pulled when the rolling update is performed."
